  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-2,1),(0,0)$ and $(2,2)$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{\u2032},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$  \n\n- $(6,-18)$\n- $(-5,-20)$\n- $(12,-24)$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 10 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 & 0 & -6 \\\\ -24 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{\u2032}$ are  $(12,-24),(0,0)$ and $(-6,12).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
